// C3.5 / ADR 0072 (negative): a call to an effecting fn in STATEMENT position.
//
// `do_work()` suspends — under the `Kont*` ABI it returns a continuation, not an
// `i64` — so discarding it in statement position needs the same frame reification a
// let-bound perform does. It is refused rather than lowered.
//
// THIS ONE IS WORTH READING TWICE, because the old behaviour was not a crash or a
// wrong number but a MISSING EFFECT. The program compiled, exited 42, and the
// handler's `print(7)` never ran: the continuation was allocated, dropped on the
// floor, and `caller` returned a pure 42 as though the perform had happened. Empty
// stdout, correct-looking exit code, no diagnostic anywhere.
//
// The mechanism is the one ADR 0072 exists to close: the gate walked for `perform`
// NODES, while the ABI substitution that creates the continuation is keyed on the
// CALLEE'S SIGNATURE. Write the identical program with `perform Io.read()` in place
// of `do_work()` and it was rejected cleanly — the two spellings failed in opposite
// directions.

effect Io {
    read() -> i64;
}

fn do_work() -> i64 ! { Io } {
    perform Io.read()
}

fn caller() -> i64 ! { Io } {
    do_work();
    42
}

fn main() -> i64 {
    handle caller() with {
        Io.read(k) => {
            print(7);
            k(42)
        }
    }
}
